        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "**Vacant Property Grant Available**\n\nRAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this superb three-bedroom end-of-terrace family home to the Finglas property market, ideally positioned on the ever-popular Cappagh Avenue. Set on an exceptionally large site and benefiting from a generous front driveway, gated side access and a substantial rear garden, No. 128 offers excellent proportions both internally and externally, together with fantastic scope for a new owner to modernise, extend or further enhance the property, subject to the necessary planning permissions.\n\nInternal accommodation briefly comprises an entrance porch leading into a welcoming entrance hallway, a bright and well-proportioned living room positioned just off the hallway and a spacious kitchen/dining room to the rear. The kitchen provides direct access to the substantial rear garden, creating excellent potential for both family living and entertaining. Upstairs there are two generous double bedrooms, both benefiting from built-in wardrobes, a well-proportioned single bedroom and a family bathroom.\n\nNo. 128 Cappagh Avenue extends to approximately c. 76 sq.m and offers bright, spacious and well-proportioned accommodation throughout. The property has been well maintained and provides a practical layout, while the impressive site offers excellent scope for a new owner to modernise and put their own stamp on the home. Additional benefits include gas-fired central heating, double glazed windows throughout, a large front driveway providing ample off-street parking, gated side access and a substantial rear garden.\n\nCappagh Avenue is within easy reach of Finglas Village and Charlestown Shopping Centre, offering an excellent selection of shops, supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, schools, sports clubs and recreational facilities. DCU, IKEA, Clearwater Shopping Centre and The National Botanic Gardens are also all within easy reach. The area is exceptionally well connected, with numerous Dublin Bus routes serving the surrounding area and providing frequent access to Dublin City Centre and beyond. The M50, N2, N3, M1 and Dublin Airport are all easily accessible, making this an ideal location for commuters.\n\nViewing is highly recommended. Contact Ray Cooke Auctioneers today on 0861985247 or 015411455 to arrange a viewing or for further information.\n\nAdditional Features:\n• BER D\n• c. 76 sq.m\n• Built 1964\n• Three-bedroom end-of-terrace family home\n• Family bathroom\n• Gas-fired central heating\n• Double glazed windows throughout\n• Large front driveway with ample off-street parking\n• Entrance porch\n• Welcoming entrance hallway\n• Bright living room\n• Large kitchen/dining room\n• Two generous double bedrooms with built-in wardrobes\n• Spacious single bedroom\n• Family bathroom\n• Large rear garden\n• Gated side access\n• Large site\n• Greenspace to front of property\n• Excellent potential to modernise and add value\n• Mature and highly sought-after residential location\n• Close to Finglas Village and Charlestown Shopping Centre\n• Excellent selection of local schools and amenities\n• Easy access to the M50, N2, N3, M1 and Dublin Airport\n• Well serviced by public transport"
      },
